bin/
obj/
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
TestResults/
# Contents rather than the directory itself: git does not descend into an excluded directory, so
# "artifacts/" would make every negation below unreachable.
artifacts/*

# Except the shipment that is current. Build output does not belong in a repository as a rule, and
# every other version stays out — but a shop asking for the software should not have to wait for
# somebody to be at the build machine. One version's worth, replaced rather than accumulated.
#
# The unzipped folders only. GitHub refuses any file over 100 MB outright, and the zips crossed it
# at 1.4.3 — the acceptance report added 2.4 MB to a 99.1 MB zip and the push was rejected. The
# folders hold the same installer at 98.8 MB, and are the more useful form here anyway: the guides
# and the feature report open in the browser instead of having to be downloaded and extracted.
#
# The installer itself is now within 1.2 MB of the same limit. When it crosses, this stops working
# and the shipment moves to a GitHub Release, where the cap is 2 GB.
!artifacts/ship/
artifacts/ship/*
!artifacts/ship/RetailPOS-GST-1.4.3/
!artifacts/ship/RetailPOS-NoTax-1.4.3/

# The assembled Pages site. Generated from artifacts/ship on every deploy, never edited.
_site/

*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
